From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:48:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: fade out the settings gear after 3 idle seconds with a
 controller

When a physical controller is connected on an iPhone or iPad screen, keeping the top-centre settings gear permanently visible distracts from the game picture and risks OLED burn-in on long sessions.

Fade the gear out after 3 idle seconds while a physical controller is connected on the device screen unless VoiceOver is running, skipping the 0.3-second fade animation when Reduce Motion is enabled, and wake it for 3 seconds on any screen touch while keeping it visible whenever the in-game menu is open. Also add the missing dm_players_reported stub to DuoRuntimeStubs.m so the DuoHarness test target links cleanly.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2003
Reason: Fade out the in-game menu gear after 3 idle seconds while a physical controller is connected on the device screen to prevent visual distraction and OLED burn-in, and wake it for 3 seconds on any screen touch.
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#809
